5pid|v|To reduce from a solid to a liquid state, as by heat; to liquefy; as, to melt wax, tallow, or lead; to melt ice or snow. ; Hence: To soften, as by a warming or kindly influence; to relax; to render gentle or susceptible to mild influences; sometimes, in a bad sense, to take away the firmness of; to weaken. ; To be changed from a solid to a liquid state under the influence of heat; as, butter and wax melt at moderate temperatures. ; To dissolve; as, sugar melts in the mouth. ; Hence: To be softened; to become tender, mild, or gentle; also, to be weakened or subdued, as by fear. ; To lose distinct form or outline; to blend. ; To disappear by being dispersed or dissipated; as, the fog melts away.	o:40gu,97,9;1xup,87,5;5ke5,82,5;5zxz,81,4;76hr,79,16;49do,73,221;1hga,71,58;9k9o,70,6;8txf,69,81;92a3,66,103;1ne3,64,2;agvk,64,15;5ram,63,27;16e3,63,32;5hd1,60,7~49do,73,221;92a3,66,103;8txf,69,81;1hga,71,58;9lnm,4,49;4n89,50,40;akx0,39,35;16e3,63,32;5r8m,36,30;76hf,45,30;3rqz,53,29;b6z,56,28;5ram,63,27;36et,14,22;3qyg,37,21	s:8txo,108,20;53ex,105,5;49du,95,4;3quz,94,14;97dt,91,3;y9t,90,6;1gbh,84,10;8opd,83,5;76hr,80,17;49fg,79,3;5w32,78,3;36kv,77,17;af2,71,7;5tv6,68,14;1zuy,63,18~49do,62,100;45xr,39,56;19qu,52,31;agmu,12,25;8txo,108,20;akx0,31,20;1zuy,63,18;36kv,77,17;76hr,80,17;40wc,17,17;8lmj,43,16;1xx1,50,14;3quz,94,14;5tv6,68,14;9h3y,42,14	d:3mdg,57,13;6x6l,48,46;rua,43,17;8rw4,41,29;4jf0,41,14;5b24,41,49;97lo,40,10;7nk2,37,64;31jk,36,61;7b0w,34,35;9kyv,32,12;16e3,23,2;2qfd,22,61;1pwi,19,51;599p,17,63~4wan,4,289;3qu,10,110;3186,3,106;7f56,11,95;8peu,15,84;7nk2,37,64;599p,17,63;2qfd,22,61;31jk,36,61;1pwi,19,51;5b24,41,49;6x6l,48,46;7b0w,34,35;8rw4,41,29;snc,5,24	D:3tz9,43,1;pfp,41,203;36et,41,140;8txf,29,5;8rw4,29,12;7nk2,28,35;8t59,27,5;6840,24,4;4d0i,20,25;1pwi,15,40;3rqz,15,2;2m9w,14,85;2qfd,14,35;16e3,13,1;8rmr,12,17~pfp,41,203;36et,41,140;2m9w,14,85;5dsp,3,46;1pwi,15,40;7nk2,28,35;2qfd,14,35;718,2,33;4d0i,20,25;anj,4,20;8rmr,12,17;7h2o,5,13;36dg,7,13;8rw4,29,12